            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tachyon"} tachyon
            mode in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+string"} open
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+string"} bosonic string
            spectrum is an indication that its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+quantum+field+theory"} effective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantum field theory
            describes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbation+theory"} perturbation
            about an
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unstable+vacuum"} unstable vacuum
            which will
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+decay"} decay
            via
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tachyon+condensation"} tachyon condensation
          %p
            It was argued in
            %a{:href => "#Sen99"} Sen 99, Section 4
            that, since the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+string"} open
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+string"} bosonic string
            technically propagates with its endpoints on the space-filling
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D25-brane"} D25-brane
            = succeed "." do
              %em tachyon vacuum
          %p
            This conjecture became famous as
            = succeed "." do
              %strong Sen’s conjecture
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+bosonic+string+field+theory"} open bosonic string field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D25-brane"} D25-brane
            is indeed gone. There were several arguments that indeed in the vicinity of this state the perturbative open string has disappeared and turned into the closed bosonic string.
          %p
            A breakthrough happened in 2005, when
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Schnabl"} Martin Schnabl
            found an analytic expression for this “tachyon vacuum” (
            %a{:href => "#Schnabl05"}> Schnabl 05
            ).
          %h3#InSuperstringTheory In superstring theory – The K-theory conjecture
          %p
            Sen’s conjecture actually originates in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring+theory"} superstring theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#Sen98"}> Sen 98
            ). While here the tachyon mode for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+string"} open
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstrings"} superstrings
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetric
            = succeed "-configurations" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+stability"} stability
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+superstring+vacua"} perturbative superstring vacua
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tachyon"} tachyon
            modes in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+string"} open
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstrings"} superstrings
            stretching between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-D-branes"} anti-D-branes
          .float_right_image{:style => "margin: -30px 0px 20px 20px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/AntiBraneAnnihilationAsKGroupEquivRelation.jpg", :width => "300px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                from
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/Equivariant+Stable+Cohomotopy+and+Branes"} Sch 18
          %p
            Here the conjecture states that the respective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tachyon+condensation"} tachyon condensation
            witnesses the annihilation of the brane/anti-brane pair (
            %a{:href => "#Sen98"}> Sen 98
            ).
          %p
            This conjectured process is one motivations for the further
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjecture"} conjecture
            that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charge"} D-brane charge
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} charge quantized
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            (
            %a{:href => "D-brane#Witten98"}> Witten 98, Section 3
            ), since this decay plausibly implements on the D-branes’s
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chan-Paton+gauge+field"} Chan-Paton
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            the defining
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            (
            %a{:href => "topological+K-theory#eq:DefiningEquivalenceRelation"}> here
            ) of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Tachyon Dynamics in Open String Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0410103"} arXiv:hep-th/0410103
          %p
            For more references in the context of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+field+theory"} string field theory
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "string+field+theory#BosonicStringVacuumAndSenConjecture"} Tachyon dynamics, decaying D-branes and Sen’s conjecture
          %h3#ReferencesForSuperstrings For superstrings
          %p
            Sen’s conjecture on the decay of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-D-brane"} anti-D-brane
            pairs in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring+theory"} superstring theory
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+string"} open
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tachyon+condensation"} tachyon condensation
          %ul
            %li#Sen98
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Tachyon Condensation on the Brane Antibrane System
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9805170"} arXiv:hep-th/9805170
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/1126-6708/1998/08/012"} doi:10.1088/1126-6708/1998/08/012
            %li#Sen99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Universality of the Tachyon Potential
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9911116"} arXiv:hep-th/9911116
          %p
            The resulting conjecture that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charge"} D-brane charge
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} charge quantized
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "D-brane#Witten98"} Witten 98, Section 3
          %p
            Discussion via
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring+field+theory"} superstring field theory
          %ul
            %li#Erler13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theodore+Erler"}> Theodore Erler
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Analytic Solution for Tachyon Condensation in Berkovits’ Open Superstring Field Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1308.4400"} arXiv:1308.4400
          %p
            which concludes (on
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1308.4400.pdf#page=32"} p. 32
          %blockquote
            %p
              It would also be interesting to see if these developments can shed light on the long-speculated relation between string field theory and the K-theoretic description of D-brane charge
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %a{:href => "D-brane#DBraneChargeQuantizationInTopologicalKTheory"} 75, 76, 77
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
          %p Similarly in
          %ul
            %li#Erler19
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theodore+Erler"}> Theodore Erler
              ,
              %em Four Lectures on Analytic Solutions in Open String Field Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1912.00521"}> arXiv:1912.00521
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/1768105"} spire:1768105
          %p
            which lists (on
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1912.00521.pdf#page=113"} p. 112
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+field+theory"} string field theory
          %blockquote
            %p Are there topological invariants of the open string star algebra representing D-brane charges?
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              E. Aldo Arroyo:
              %em A New Real Tachyon Vacuum Solution in Cubic Superstring Field Theory
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.16656"}> arXiv:2503.16656
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#for_bosonic_strings For bosonic strings
          %p
            The conjecture for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+strings"} bosonic strings
            originates with
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#Sen99"} Sen 99, Section 4
          %p An analytic check was found in
          %ul
            %li#Schnabl05
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Schnabl"}> Martin Schnabl
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Analytic solution for tachyon condensation in open string field theory
              %p
                Volume 10, Number 4 (2006), 433-501. (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0511286"}> arXiv:hep-th/0511286
                )
            %li#EllwoodSchnabl06
              %p
                Ian Ellwood,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Schnabl"} Martin Schnabl
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Proof of vanishing cohomology at the tachyon vacuum
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0606142"} arXiv:hep-th/0606142
        .revisedby
